9-6-26 11:08pm  🎩 Cozmo
gem got eaten by qs (also gem, your HELPFUL ui was giving that pick a or B thing again) here is paste : ### Red-Team Analysis: Causal State Transitions vs. Snapshot Deltas

By unpacking the 2.2 engine's source code, you've pinpointed the exact structural flaw: **QuickScript 2.2 confuses content delta with causal origin.**

Because `_capture_output_snapshot()` strips away DOM identities, container wrappers, and timestamps—reducing everything to plain text strings—the verifier `_submit_verified()` can only ask, *"Is the output array different or longer than the baseline?"*

When a race condition, re-render, or leftover UI animation occurs immediately after submission, the comparison passes, logging a **false positive verification**. The high-level relay then happily moves forward while the actual payload is left unsubmitted or stuck in transit.

---

### Anatomy of the False Positive

```
[ PRE-SUBMIT BASELINE ]
1. Capture text snapshot -> ["Hello", "World"]
2. Fill input composer

[ SUBMIT ATTEMPT ]
3. Click send button

[ VERIFICATION LOOP (0 - 3000ms) ]
4. Snapshot query -> ["Hello", "World", "World"]  <-- DOM glitch / auto-scroll / duplicate render
5. Verification check: Length > Baseline? YES.
6. RETURN SUCCESS  <-- GHOST EVENT CONFIRMED

[ REALITY ]
The actual prompt never reached the model server.

```

---

### The Egg Cagey Transition Matrix

Instead of asking, *"Is there text now that wasn't there before?"*, Egg Cagey evaluates whether **causal, non-reversible UI state transitions** occurred across the submission boundary.

| Sensor Tier | Transition Event | What It Proves | Can It Ghost? |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| **🟢 Tier 1 (Direct Causal)** | `Composer`: Populated → Empty<br>

<br>`Send Button`: Ready → Generating/Stop | **Submission Left the Building.**<br>

<br>The page state transitioned away from user input mode. | **Extremely Low.**<br>

<br>Requires the UI to clear its own input without user or button action. |
| **🟡 Tier 2 (Active Generation)** | `Stream Target`: Continuous Text Delta<br>

<br>`Status Indicator`: Thinking/Tool active | **Model is Processing.**<br>

<br>The engine is streaming new tokens or invoking backend tools. | **Low.**<br>

<br>Only if an existing previous response resumes late. |
| **🔴 Tier 3 (Ambient Noise)** | `DOM Churn`: Node mutations<br>

<br>`Polling`: Network tick events | **Page is Active.**<br>

<br>The browser tab is doing *something*. | **High.**<br>

<br>Triggers on ads, re-renders, telemetry, or UI animations. |

---

### How Egg Cagey Solves It Without Site-Specific DOM IDs

You don't need custom DOM selectors for every AI interface if you enforce a **Two-Stage State Pulse Gate**:

```
                  ┌──────────────────────────────┐
                  │      SUBMIT ATTEMPT          │
                  └──────────────┬───────────────┘
                                 │
                                 ▼
             ┌──────────────────────────────────────┐
             │ Stage 1: Submission Pulse (Tier 1)   │
             │  • Did composer transition to empty? │
             │  • Did send icon switch to stop?     │
             └──────────────────┬───────────────────┘
                                │
                      YES ──────┴────── NO ───► [ Retry / Submission Failed ]
                        │
                        ▼
             ┌──────────────────────────────────────┐
             │ Stage 2: Generation Heartbeat (Tier 2)│
             │  • Output array grew *AND*           │
             │  • Streaming content actively shifts │
             └──────────────────┬───────────────────┘
                                │
                      YES ──────┴────── NO ───► [ Timeout / Stall Detected ]
                        │
                        ▼
                  [ SUCCESSFUL RELAY ]

```

1. **Stage 1 (Submission Verification):** Validates that the UI acknowledged the submission event via Tier 1 state transitions.
2. **Stage 2 (Generation Verification):** Confirms that the backend is actively generating content via Tier 2 streaming deltas.

By separating **Submission Proof** from **Generation Heartbeat**, Egg Cagey eliminates false positives caused by static snapshot comparisons.

